Revision history for Test-Mutation

0.001
    - Measure Perl modules and commands in per-job copies of the distribution.
    - Build XS distributions in the measurement copy and trace tests through child interpreters.
    - Record the test that detected a mutant after confirming that it passes with the original source.
    - Reuse verified results and unmodified test runs when their inputs match.
    - Reject shard merges when compiler inputs or the driver's parser versions differ.
    - Open a mutant's diff by identifier from the SQLite index and inspect its last measured verdict.
    - Apply the same score threshold to runs, merged shards, and Perl assertions.
    - After adding a test, use `mutation run --undetected` to recheck surviving and uncovered mutants.
    - Pass `--enable early-exit` to include guarded exits in the default profile.
    - Publish results in the terminal, schema-compatible JSON, a single HTML file, and GitHub Actions summaries.
    - Read the command, configuration, diagnostic, and mutator reference with perldoc mutation.
